However, the exponent 10^{sum_{j=k+1 to N} L_j} depends on the numbers that come after position k. So for a fixed position k and a fixed number i in position k, the exponent is the sum of the digit lengths of the numbers in positions k+1 to N. But since the numbers after k are a permutation of the remaining N-1 numbers, the sum of their digit lengths is fixed for a given set of numbers.

